From 58b67d2adb723948f99e6b78bbfc3c59b4881edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:04:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] vr: allow NixOS graphics drivers in the Linux XR sandbox

NixOS exposes its Vulkan drivers through /run/opengl-driver, with
libraries and manifests in /nix/store. The XR sandbox cannot read them,
so entering VR fails even when isSessionSupported() succeeds.

Allow reads of the driver profile and the store directories it points
to. Preload driver libraries before enabling seccomp to load their
dependencies. Keep other store packages inaccessible and leave the FHS
paths unchanged.

Simulate NixOS on Ubuntu/AMD RADV in a container: place Vulkan ICDs and
libraries under /nix/store, link them through /run/opengl-driver, and
hide the FHS manifests and libraries. Run Chromium against Monado with
--enable-features=OpenXR, without and with the fix. Check that VR
renders with Chromium's sandbox enabled.
This does not test native NixOS or NVIDIA.

Bug: 506004811
Change-Id: Id7dd74b4f10e554868ed8ddef6d5d88c2a81a29b
